{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3793270/extras/dee6707f5a3eef50c18ba3b0cda65a02.avif?t=1757788058\" data-has-big width=800 height=450 /></span> <br><strong>Bygoner</strong> is a non-linear \u201croad movie\u201d set in a medieval world. A nameless knight travels across the southern lands of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania (modern-day Ukraine) in the early 16th century.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game consists of small story-driven novellas connected to the inhabitants of the frontier, while the main storyline focuses on the protagonist\u2019s psychological state, enriched with visions and the mythical worldview of a medieval mind.\u00a0<strong>Bygoner</strong> is a fictional word inspired by the Old English saying <i>\u201clet bygones be bygones\u201d</i>. It embodies the idea of someone who leaves everything behind.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At its core, the game focuses on exploration, interwoven with combat encounters. There is also an element of resource management essential for the journey. The player chooses their path, unlocking new areas of the world with unique events and locations.<br><br> <strong>\u0421urrent development roadmap looks like this:</strong><br><strong>2023</strong> \u2013 Development begins</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2025</strong> \u2013 Steam page goes live</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Late 2025 / Early 2026</strong> \u2013 Alpha demo release</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2026</strong> \u2013 Early Access launch</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>2026\u20132028</strong> \u2013 Ongoing Early Access support before full release<br><strong>2028</strong> \u2013 Full game release*<br><br>*Dates and milestones are subject to change as development progresses.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3793270?t=1757788058","backgroun